  "summary": "Twenty per-backend settings modules (bigquery, clickhouse, databricks, druid, duckdb, exasol, impala, materialize, motherduck, mssql, mysql, oracle, postgresql, pyspark, redshift, risingwave, singlestoredb, snowflake, sqlite, trino). Each declares a <NAME>_SPEC BackendSpec with provider_type, ibis_dialect, optional default_port and connection_string_scheme, supported_auth, and a ParameterSpec list mapping uppercase fields to driver keys, plus a @register-decorated *BackendProfile subclass. Some add field validators (BigQuery project id, DuckDB memory limit, Redshift region and role ARN), backend-specific enums, __adapters__ config shaping (MSSQL, MySQL, Snowflake) or a to_url_parts override (MotherDuck). MotherDuck rides on duckdb and Redshift rides on postgres; PySpark and Databricks have no URL scheme.",
